 far eastern West Haven, on the north side of Main Road, a short way west of"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d03", "start": 0, "end": 36, "text": "taking up most of the second floor ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d03", "start": 37, "end": 135, "text": "An ell extends to the left , dating to a 1920s renovation done after a fire damaged an older ell ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d03", "start": 136, "end": 309, "text": "[ 2 ] The house was built in 1798-1800 for Simeon Smith , a wealthy businessman who had moved to the area ( then part of Fair Haven ) in 1787 from northwestern Connecticut ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d03", "start": 310, "end": 388, "text": "Smith 's relationship with the designer William Sprat is not well understood ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d03", "start": 389, "end": 508, "text": "Sprat was active in the Litchfield , Connecticut area , and was apparently hired by Smith to at least draw up plans for"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d04", "start": 0, "end": 105, "text": "in addition to providing medical services, serving as a local probate judge and in the state legislature."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d04", "start": 106, "end": 228, "text": "Simeon Smith Mansion The Simeon Smith Mansion is a historic farm property on Smith (or Doran) Road in West Haven, Vermont."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d04", "start": 229, "end": 383, "text": "The property, more than includes a farmhouse dating to the 1790s, which was the seat of Simeon Smith, a prominent local doctor, politician, and landowner."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0448-71f44b761912:d04", "start": 384, "end": 460, "text": "The property was listed on t